  "scope": "One disposable Kind cluster on Kubernetes v1.36.1 hosts two synthetic worker Pods, one observer Pod, and one case-owned ClusterIP aggregation mock. The mock has an Kubernetes TokenReview verification of audience-scoped Pod identities, an enrollment-to-round table, and accepts only a fixed v1 JSON schema with three finite numeric entries in [-0.05, 0.05] when enforcement is enabled. Red sends only harmless synthetic metadata and small numeric values: one enrolled worker on the wrong assigned round and one short numeric vector. Green repeats those requests after enforcement is enabled, then two assigned workers submit ordinary fixed vectors. An independent observer reads stable counters and the exact mock aggregate. No real model, training framework, external service, real identity, external credential, feed, or target is used. A separate authenticated observer can read counters and is refused ordinary contribution access.",
